new file mode 100644
index 0000000..8a1415a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/examples/ALFA/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,66 @@
+# ALFA Delphes card with ARC particle identification
+
+Files added to Delphes:
+
+| File | What |
+|---|---|
+| `modules/ARCPID.h`, `modules/ARCPID.cc` | per-track Cherenkov emulation of the ARC (gas + aerogel), chi2 PID |
+| `classes/DelphesClasses.h/.cc` | 16 new members on `Candidate` and `Track` (see below); `ClassDef` versions bumped |
+| `modules/TreeWriter.cc` | fills the new `Track` members |
+| `modules/ModulesLinkDef.h` | registers `ARCPID` |
+| `cards/delphes_card_ALFA.tcl` | the ALFA card (3 T, all-MAPS tracker, ARC, GRAiNITA ECAL) |
+| `examples/ALFA/gun_{pip,kp,p}.cmnd` | Pythia8 single-particle guns, log-uniform p in 0.1-60 GeV, abs(eta) < 2.6 |
+| `examples/ALFA/arc_separation.py` | separation power and confusion matrix from the output |
+
+## Build
+
+```bash
+# key4hep stack gives ROOT, Pythia8, HepMC
+source /cvmfs/sw-nightlies.hsf.org/key4hep/setup.sh
+./configure          # regenerates the Makefile so the new module is picked up
+make -j8 HAS_PYTHIA8=true
+# or: mkdir build && cd build && cmake .. && make -j8
+```
+
+## Run
+
+```bash
+./DelphesPythia8 cards/delphes_card_ALFA.tcl examples/ALFA/gun_kp.cmnd  kp.root
+./DelphesPythia8 cards/delphes_card_ALFA.tcl examples/ALFA/gun_pip.cmnd pip.root
+./DelphesPythia8 cards/delphes_card_ALFA.tcl examples/ALFA/gun_p.cmnd   p.root
+python3 examples/ALFA/arc_separation.py --pi pip.root --k kp.root --p p.root --out plots
+```
+
+Expected with the first-pass parameters (ARCPID study, July 2026): pi/K >= 3 sigma up to ~14 GeV (aerogel) and ~38 GeV (gas); K/p to ~23 GeV (aerogel) and ~64 GeV (gas); confusion between pi and K only above ~38 GeV.
+
+## Track members
+
+```
+Track.CherenkovAngleGas / CherenkovAngleAerogel         true Cherenkov angle [rad], -1 if no ring
+Track.CherenkovRecoAngleGas / CherenkovRecoAngleAerogel measured (smeared) angle [rad], -1 if no ring
+Track.SigmaThetaCGas / SigmaThetaCAerogel               per-track angular resolution [rad]
+Track.NpeGas / NpeAerogel                               expected photo-electrons (stored even below MinPe)
+Track.ARCchi2Pi / ARCchi2K / ARCchi2P                   per-hypothesis chi2, -1 if no ring
+Track.ARCpid                                            +-211 / +-321 / +-2212 (smallest chi2), 0 if no ring
+Track.ARCprobPi / ARCprobK / ARCprobP                   hypothesis probabilities exp(-chi2/2), normalised to 1 (equal priors), -1 if no ring
+Track.ARCmass                                           mass of the best hypothesis [GeV], -1 if no ring
+```
+
+Hard PID: cut on `ARCpid` (or use `ARCmass` as the track mass with 100% weight). Soft PID: the probabilities, e.g. a track that is 5% pi / 90% K / 5% p carries `ARCprobPi = 0.05, ARCprobK = 0.90, ARCprobP = 0.05`; kaon enrichment with `ARCprobK > 0.9` or `ARCchi2K < ARCchi2Pi - 4`. Equal priors are assumed; multiply by your own priors (e.g. pi:K:p ~ 0.8:0.1:0.1 in Z jets) and renormalise if needed.
+
+## The algorithm (per track)
+
+1. Region: a track is in the barrel if its straight-line extrapolation reaches r = BarrelRmin at |z| <= BarrelZmax, otherwise in an endcap if it crosses |z| = EndcapZmin at EndcapRmin <= r <= EndcapRmax. Curlers (2 R_curv < BarrelRmax) get nothing.
+2. Path length: L = t / sin(theta) in the barrel, t / |cos(theta)| in the endcap, with t the radiator thickness (full cell depth for every covered track).
+3. True angle: cos(theta_c) = 1 / (n beta) from the true mass and momentum; no ring below threshold.
+4. Yield: N_pe = N_sat (L/L_ref) sin^2(theta_c) / sin^2(theta_c,max). A ring is usable if N_pe >= MinPe and it passes the ring-finding efficiency formula.
+5. Resolution: per photon sigma_1^2 = sigma_single^2 + sigma_chrom^2 with the chromatic term sigma_chrom = (dn/dE * sigma_E) / (n tan theta_c) from the card's `GasDnDe`/`GasSigmaE` (and the aerogel equivalents; 0 = folded into sigma_single); plus a bending term sigma_bend = BendingCoefficient * 0.3 B L sin(theta) / p (the track direction changes across the radiator in the field; 1/sqrt(12) for uniform emission, ~4 mrad per photon at 10 GeV in 15 cm of gas at 3 T); per track sigma = sqrt(sigma_1^2 / N_pe + SigmaTrack^2); measured angle = true + Gauss(sigma).
+6. PID: for h in {pi, K, p} at the smeared momentum, chi2_h = sum over radiators of ((measured - theta_h)/sigma_h)^2. A measured ring where h predicts none adds (measured/sigma)^2; no ring where h predicts N_h photons adds 2 N_h. Smallest chi2 wins.
+
+## Parameters to calibrate on the k4geo full simulation
+
+Per radiator: `n` (from the material at the detected-spectrum-weighted energy), `dn/dE` at that energy and `sigma_E` of the detected spectrum (chromatic term), `N_sat` (yield at beta = 1, normal incidence, L = L_ref, after PDE and mirror reflectivity), `sigma_single` (per-track sigma times sqrt(N_pe)). Then the efficiency formulas (barrel-endcap crack at |cos theta| ~ 0.73, ring-off-sensor losses) and `SigmaTrack`. The ALFA ARC task board (tasks T05/T06) produces them in this format.
+
+## Known simplifications
+
+Single-radiator smearing only (no photon-level simulation, no background hits, no cell boundaries), straight-line region assignment, constant sigma_single. The HCAL resolution in the card is a placeholder. The tracker endcap layout follows the July 2026 ALFA card; the engineering design is in progress.
